What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../bringup_status
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		"power-domain-only" for the experimental T8140 ANE driver.
		With enable_engine_power=1, reports "engine-power-and-ce".
		This opts into manual ANE CPU/subblock power sequencing and
		the H17 CE initialization handshake during runtime resume.
		Firmware, DART and command execution remain unimplemented in
		this Linux driver; neither status establishes inference support.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../inference_available
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Always 0 for this driver version. No accelerator character
		device, inference ioctl, or CPU fallback is provided.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../cluster_range
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Hexadecimal physical base and byte length of the validated
		J700 ANE cluster resource. This range includes DART apertures;
		the driver does not reserve, map or access it.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../runtime_transitions
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		"resume=N suspend=N" counts driver runtime PM callbacks since
		probe. These are not ANE computation or firmware counters.
		The standard power/control interface holds ANE_SYS on with
		"on" and releases it with "auto". ANE_SYS power alone does
		not initialize the ANE engine.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../power_state
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Experimental T8140 PMGR diagnostic, available only when the
		module is loaded with enable_power_snapshot=1. Otherwise reads
		fail with EOPNOTSUPP. Format:
		"sys=0xXXXXXXXX cpu=0xXXXXXXXX subblocks=0xXXXXXXXX".
		Reads existing shared PMGR syscon offsets 0x290, 0xc000 and
		0xc008, respectively. Each is a raw 32-bit register value;
		bits 3:0 are requested state and bits 7:4 are actual state.
		0 is power gated, 4 clock gated, and 15 active.
		Reads do not power up the ANE or access its cluster aperture.
		The three reads are sequential, not an atomic snapshot, and
		their values do not establish firmware or compute readiness.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../ce_initializations
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Number of completed CE initialization handshakes since probe.
		Always zero unless enable_engine_power=1. Reads return a cached
		counter without waking the device or accessing engine registers.
		This is not a firmware, command completion or inference counter.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/401600040.ane-fw-test/start_bootstrap
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Separate experimental firmware backend, present only with the
		ordered RAM test overlays. Write exactly "25G83" once to start
		the locally pinned firmware after memory/power/DAPF validation.
		Loading the module alone does not start firmware. Once started,
		DMA, power and module references are retained until a Neo reboot.
		This is a bounded bring-up interface, not a stable userspace ABI.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/401600040.ane-fw-test/test_compute
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Present only when a SHA-pinned numerical case was built into the
		experimental firmware backend. Requires completed startup and
		accepts one attempt per boot. The original case accepts "conv16";
		the separately compiled tiny language-model case accepts
		"anemll-tiny". Each build accepts only its own action/package.
		The tiny case performs three autoregressive transformer/head
		jobs with CPU embedding lookup and greedy token selection.
		Every output is poisoned before submission and compared with a
		validated reference outside the ANE IOMMU domain. A failed job
		retains all mappings until reboot; it must not be retried live.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/401600040.ane-fw-test/status
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Cached experimental firmware state and counters:
		"state=... error=N started=N allocations=N shared_bytes=N
		samples_passed=N shutdown_reply=N" on one line. Completion
		requires three passed samples and a shutdown reply. The reply
		does not establish safe hot unload or suspend; reboot still
		ends the retained test lifetime. No arbitrary model API exists.

What:		/dev/aurora-ane0
Date:		September 2026
Description:
		Private experimental application interface, only in the
		SHA-pinned tiny ANEMLL model build. Mode0600; CAP_SYS_RAWIO
		required at open and every ioctl. Only one open owner; legacy
		sysfs mutations return EBUSY while that owner exists. Structures
		and command numbers are in the private apple-ane-user.h header;
		this is not a stable upstream userspace ABI.
		INFO returns cached capability/state/counters. LOAD starts the
		pinned firmware and program. RUN copies one finite 4096-byte
		input and returns 32768-byte logits with completion metadata.
		There is no userspace DMA mapping or arbitrary-command input.
		The model is fixed; input tensors are application supplied.
		Sessions have at most 256 jobs. Bad validation/input reads do
		not submit work. A copyback EFAULT can follow a completed job;
		INFO still counts it, and callers must account for that before
		retrying. Protocol/firmware failures block further submissions
		and retain mappings. SHUTDOWN or final fd close requests native
		program/firmware shutdown. DMA, power and module references
		remain pinned until a Neo-only reboot. Normal unload, suspend
		and automatic engine reset are not implemented.
